## Per-directory licensing

This repository mixes code, prose and hardware designs. The MIT text above
applies to software. Other parts are licensed as follows:

| Path | License | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `src/`, `scripts/` | **MIT** | as above |
| `docs/`, `README*.md`, `ETHICS.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md` | **CC BY 4.0** | https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ |
| `docs/assets/*.svg` | **CC BY 4.0** | figures, attribution required |
| `hardware/` (BOM, future CAD) | **CERN-OHL-S v2** | https://ohwr.org/cern_ohl_s_v2.txt |

If you reuse the hardware design, CERN-OHL-S v2 requires that modifications to
the design files be shared under the same license. Using the design to build a
rig for yourself is unrestricted.

## Third-party notices

The repository references, but does not bundle, the following projects. Their
licenses apply when you install or copy them:

- **GRBL** — GPL-3.0 (firmware for the Arduino UNO motion controller)
- **Arduino core / ESP32 Arduino core** — LGPL-2.1 / Apache-2.0
- **OpenCV** — Apache-2.0
- **ESP32 BLE HID libraries** (e.g. `ESP32-BLE-Mouse`, `ESP32-BLE-Keyboard`) — MIT

The MIT/CC-BY/CERN-OHL split above does not relicense any third-party code.
